      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(ui): move Devices into Settings and redesign the device inventory",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Devices page lived as a top-level workspace destination even though it is fleet/system configuration, and its layout had accumulated visual debt: three header buttons at three different heights, a redundant card title repeating the page title, a manual Refresh button on a page that already receives live presence events, plain-text rows with no visual anchor, and low-contrast \"muted div\" section separators that made pending approvals easy to miss.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDevices is now a Settings page (System group, `/settings/devices`, with `/nodes` kept as a route alias so old links and the e2e path keep working). The inventory card was redesigned around a per-device identity tile: a form-factor icon (phone / browser / terminal / machine, gateway gets a server glyph) derived from the shared gateway client id/mode contract, with the connectivity dot anchored to the tile. Sections (Pending approval, Paired, Connected without pairing) use proper labels, header actions are two equal-height buttons (stale cleanup + pair), and the static card subtitle became a live \"N of M connected · K awaiting approval\" summary. The manual Refresh button is gone: the page already refreshes via presence/pairing gateway events plus a 30s poll, so the button was redundant surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDevices now lives where users expect fleet management (Settings → Devices, searchable from settings search), pending pairing requests stand out, every device row is scannable at a glance by device type and status, and there is no confusing manual Refresh button — the list stays current on its own. Old `/nodes` URLs continue to work.\n\n## Evidence\n\nDark mode (mock harness, full page):\n\n![devices settings dark](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/2026-07-devices-settings/devices-settings-dark.png)\n\nLight mode:\n\n![devices settings light](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/2026-07-devices-settings/devices-settings-light.png)\n\n- Verified in the mock harness (`pnpm dev:ui:mock`): settings sidebar entry + new `monitorSmartphone` icon, icon tiles (server/monitor/smartphone/terminal/globe), section labels, equal-height header actions, `/nodes` alias routing, and that the workspace sidebar \"More\" menu no longer lists Devices.\n- Locale bundles regenerated with authenticated `pnpm ui:i18n:sync` (fallbacks=0 for all locales).\n- Unit tests updated: `app-navigation` route/icon tables, settings-group pin-drop coverage, `view.devices` render tests; `mobile-pairing` e2e asserts the new `/settings/devices` path.\n",
        "branch": "claude/devices-page-redesign-221ff2",
